  "$schema": "qsurv.sprites.v0",
  "notes": "Frame sources for packed-sprite art. Validated by tools/test-art.mjs (paths + sheet geometry + hero + enemy footprints). Loaded by js/art/load.js in the browser only. One entry per engine slot; strip = horizontal frame range of the source sheet. sheet = the engine footprint the built sheet must keep (test-boot 26.3 / 33.4.3 tables). render.artH = final art height in px (scale derived), render.trim = [x,y,w,h] crop for static battlers, render.head = [cx,top] in source-cell coords for the baseball overlay, recolour 'seat' = CFG.ghostColors paletteSwap ladder. A 'walk' strip (where the pack has real walk frames) feeds run[4]; without it run[4] reuses the idle frames + the ±1px bob derived in heroes.js. Enemy entries (33.4.3): frames = engine frame count (strip frames cycled + integer-px bob offsets where the source is static or shorter); facing 'right' = right-facing contract (every source was viewed before wiring; symmetric front-facing art is flip-invariant and satisfies it; a LEFT-facing source carries render.flip and bakeInto mirrors it); recolour 'elite' = gold skin path via palette.eliteColor + lumaTintMap (enemies.js keeps the gold-diamond tell; eliteFrames are the skin half); enemy.wolf.pack = per-coat wolfpack block (bigger footprint + own bob) tinted from PACK_PALS in characters.js. Boss entries (33.4.4: enemy.wraith, enemy.ryu) keep the exact engine footprints (92x112/r20, 96x112/r20, 2 frames) and declare NO recolour — D105 rolls elite on non-bosses only. Large sprites may use guest-dialect sources downscaled ≤2× (PLAN-FORK §2). 'skin.<level>.<slot>' entries (skin.m02.wolf) are per-level re-skins of common slots: same footprint/frames as the base slot, own source strip, and the same 'elite' marker.",
